## 2026-06-23 — Spawn-overlap fling bug (player "spawned at the arena edge")

- **Symptom**: In TrainingArena the player spawned at centre (0,1.5,0) but was
  flung ~29m to the arena wall within the first physics tick.
- **Root cause**: `EnemyController.Spawn` (and `PlayerController.Spawn`) called
  `parent.AddChild(e)` BEFORE `e.Position = pos`. The physics body therefore
  existed at the origin for its first tick — overlapping the player — and when
  it snapped to its real position, Godot's moving-platform logic dragged the
  player (standing on it) along until the wall stopped them.
- **Fix**: set `Position` (local, valid outside the tree) BEFORE `AddChild` in
  both Spawn methods. Rule of thumb: never AddChild a physics body at a
  placeholder position.
- **Also fixed**: TrainingArena death-cam set `GlobalPosition` before AddChild
  (is_inside_tree error on every death) — reordered. Arena trimesh floor
  collision disabled in training (coplanar duplicate of the solid box floor).

